{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>I said: I would make an end of them, I would obliterate their memory from mankind.</b> Rashi explained \"אַפְאֵיהֶם\" as: I said I would make them ownerless like פֵּאָה. But is פֵּאָה alone ownerless? Are not gleanings, forgotten sheaves, and פֵּאָה all ownerless? And why did he single out פֵּאָה specifically? And it appears that he mentioned here פֵּאָה and שִׁכְחָה, for \"אַפְאֵיהֶם\" is פֵּאָה, \"אַשְׁבִּיתָה מֵאֱנוֹשׁ זִכְרָם\" is שִׁכְחָה, for if He obliterates their memory so that no one remembers them — behold, they are ownerless like שִׁכְחָה, in which the owner of the house has no share in פֵּאָה and שִׁכְחָה; so too in the place where it says \"כִּי חֵלֶק ה׳ עַמּוֹ\" — I would remove them from before My face, for My name would no longer be called upon them. But לֶקֶט he did not mention, for the Sages said (Pe'ah 6:5): two stalks are לֶקֶט, three are not לֶקֶט, and here the scattered ones will be more than two; therefore the rule of לֶקֶט, which is forbidden to its owners, does not apply to them, but rather the Holy One, blessed be He, is destined to gather them, as it says (Isaiah 27:12): ״וְאַתֶּם תְּלֻקְּטוּ לְאַחַד אֶחָד״ etc." "And the fact that it says ״תְּלֻקְּטוּ״ in the pual (passive) construction implies through the agency of another, for they will be gathered through King Messiah. And since two in one place constitutes לֶקֶט, therefore they will be gathered specifically through King Messiah, of whom it says (Zechariah 9:9): ״עָנִי וְרֹכֵב עַל חֲמוֹר״, and a poor person is permitted in the לֶקֶט of one by one, that is, two stalks, which constitutes לֶקֶט; therefore it says: ״וְאַתֶּם תְּלֻקְּטוּ לְאַחַד אֶחָד״ — that is, two. But when the scattered ones are many, more than two in one place, then the Holy One, blessed be He, the Owner of the entire world, will gather them Himself and in His own glory, blessed be He; this is what it says (Isaiah 17:5): ״וּזְרֹעוֹ שִׁבֳּלִים יִקְצוֹר וְהָיָה כִּמְלַקֵּט שִׁבֳּלִים בְּעֵמֶק רְפָאִים״ — implying that the Holy One, blessed be He, with His own arm will gather them, not through the agency of another, because there it does not mention ״לְאַחַד אֶחָד״, implying that those gathered are more than two in one place, and they never left the domain of the Owner of the house. And this is a correct and precious allusion."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:16:10.707169753Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}